1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,710
Alex: A screenshot can be real—and still mislead you.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:10,800
Maya: Try this made-up example. Crop a sentence after “I agree,” and hide the part that says “with neither claim.”

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:21,980
Alex: Same words. Different meaning. Now imagine a post accusing Jewish people of something, using one cropped quote as the whole argument.

4
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:33,860
Maya: Before sharing it, open the original. Who said it? When? What came before and after? Are we seeing a quote, a translation, or somebody’s caption?

5
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:44,220
Alex: Then check an independent source. And even if one person really said something awful, that does not make an entire community responsible.

6
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:53,020
Maya: Context isn’t an excuse. It’s how you figure out what actually happened, and who actually did it.

7
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,790
Alex: Zoom out before you call it proof.

